Description: v3d: keep CMA for buffers a non-GPU engine actually walks
 On BCM2711/BCM2712 nothing in front of the display, codec or camera blocks is
 an IOMMU: the HVS scans out from a physical address and the VPU / rpivid /
 unicam V4L2 devices are videobuf2-dma-contig. Those buffers must be physically
 contiguous, i.e. CMA. v3d has its own MMU, so buffers that are only rendered,
 textured or read by the CPU do not.
 .
 The backend routed every buffer carrying BO_USE_SW_MASK or BO_USE_LINEAR into
 CMA as well. On a Pi that pool is a small fixed reservation (cma-512) and is at
 the same time the only source of scanout memory, so ordinary GPU and CPU
 buffers filled and fragmented it until a 4K framebuffer (32 MiB in one piece)
 could no longer be allocated -- the ARC kiosk app on a 4K display came up with
 every window state reporting "visible" and drew nothing, because
 GraphicBufferAllocator was failing at 3840x2160.
 .
 Split the single mask into three: what must be contiguous, what must fail
 loudly if it cannot be, and what must stay linear regardless of placement.
 .
 On Android the scanout half of the contiguous set is empty. fydroid's
 SurfaceFlinger is built with a factory that swaps HWComposer for a Wayland
 composer and no hwcomposer HAL is packaged, so Android never programs a KMS
 plane -- yet cros_gralloc_helpers.cc maps GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER to
 BO_USE_SCANOUT and SurfaceFlinger sets it on essentially every layer (the
 surface that failed had usage 0xb00). Honouring SCANOUT therefore put every ARC
 window buffer in CMA. This cannot be fixed in cros_gralloc_helpers.cc under
 #ifdef DRV_V3D: fydroid-rt_arm64 builds rockchip, v3d, vc4 and realtek into one
 image, and the other backends do drive real scanout hardware.
 .
 Buffers that leave CMA keep DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR + V3D_TILING_RASTER -- only
 their placement changes, not the layout their user already agreed to. UIF stays
 restricted to pure-GPU buffers. Scanout/cursor stay a soft requirement off
 Android: if CMA is exhausted they fall back to pageable memory and get GPU
 composited rather than returning -ENOMEM. Codec and camera have no fallback.
 .
 Mirrors the host-side CrOS patch v3d-cma-only-for-display-buffers.patch
 (baseboard-rpi3/media-libs/minigbm), adapted for the container: the per-BO path
 logs stay drv_logv (compiled out under NDEBUG) rather than #ifdef DEBUG, and
 V3D_LINEAR_USE is spelled out rather than derived from the contiguous set, so
 narrowing CMA can never narrow linearity.
 .
 Verified: builds clean for fydroid-rt_armv8 (rpi4, Cortex-A72) and
 fydroid-rt_arm64 (rpi5); a temporary _Static_assert harness confirmed SCANOUT is
 out of the contiguous set on Android, still in the linear set, and that the
 codec and camera flags stay contiguous. Confirmed on rpi4-fydeos-io that the
 container takes the dma-heap path ("v3d: using CMA dma-heap
 /dev/dma_heap/linux,cma"), unlike Chrome on the same board, which falls back to
 the vc4 borrow.
 .
 Measured on rpi4-fydeos-io at 3840x2160, cold boot, ARC container up and parked
 on the Chrome bridge (SurfaceFlinger + graphics allocator running, no user
 session):
 .
   stock gralloc,   login idle:  CmaFree 156428 kB
   patched gralloc, login idle:  CmaFree 286004 kB   (~129.6 MB more free CMA)
 .
 Controls: same container process set, same DRM mode (crtc-pos 3840x2160), both
 arms from a cold reboot, each reading stable across repeated samples within its
 boot, and each arm provably running its own build (the v3d_open_cma_heap log
 line number differs between them). The login screen is a valid measurement point
 for the container even though it is not one for Chrome: ARC's SurfaceFlinger and
 HALs start with the container and allocate before any session exists, and those
 allocations are exactly the GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER ones this patch diverts.
 .
 Caveats: n=1 per arm, and an earlier naive comparison of two kiosk-running reads
 was discarded because the login-idle baseline moved 166 MB between them (CMA is
 not fully returned when a kiosk session ends -- a separate defect, not addressed
 here). Still open: a repeat of the baseline, the kiosk-running arm, and one
 behavioural question -- on a manually launched kiosk, Chrome's "waiting for app
 window" splash closed on stock but was still up ~30 s in on patched. ARC itself
 reported mHasSurface=true / mDrawState=HAS_DRAWN with zero GraphicBufferAllocator
 failures on both arms, so this is not an allocation failure, but it is unresolved
 and should be settled before this ships to a product.
diff --git a/v3d.c b/v3d.c
--- a/v3d.c
+++ b/v3d.c
@@ -27,21 +27,78 @@
 #define CROS_CALLOC (1<<6)
 
 /*
- * Option A prototype: allocate scanout/shared/CPU-visible buffers from a CMA
- * dma-buf heap and import the resulting dma-buf into v3d via standard PRIME,
- * instead of borrowing a CMA BO from vc4 through the custom VC4_CALLOC ioctl
- * flag (v3d_vc4_bind.c). The heap-backed buffer is contiguous + linear, so it
- * is both HVS-scanout-capable (vc4 imports it) and v3d-renderable (v3d maps it
- * into the GPU MMU via gem_prime_import_sg_table -> v3d_bo_create_finish).
- *
- * Pure-GPU (non-shared) buffers keep their native UIF-tiled v3d allocation.
+ * Allocate contiguous buffers from a CMA dma-buf heap and import the resulting
+ * dma-buf into v3d via standard PRIME, instead of borrowing a CMA BO from vc4
+ * through the custom VC4_CALLOC ioctl flag (v3d_vc4_bind.c). The heap-backed
+ * buffer is contiguous + linear, so it is both HVS-scanout-capable (vc4 imports
+ * it) and v3d-renderable (v3d maps it into the GPU MMU via
+ * gem_prime_import_sg_table -> v3d_bo_create_finish).
  *
  * If no CMA heap is available at runtime, we fall back to the legacy
  * VC4_CALLOC borrow so behaviour never regresses.
  */
-#define V3D_HEAP_USE                                                                               \
-	(BO_USE_SW_MASK | BO_USE_SCANOUT | BO_USE_LINEAR | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER |                \
-	 BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER)
+
+/*
+ * Which buffers actually have to come out of CMA.
+ *
+ * BCM2711/BCM2712 put no IOMMU in front of the codec and camera blocks: the
+ * VPU / rpivid / unicam V4L2 devices are all videobuf2-dma-contig, so buffers
+ * those engines walk must be physically contiguous, which on a Pi means CMA.
+ * They have no software fallback either, so a failure here must be loud.
+ *
+ * v3d itself has an MMU, so a buffer that is only rendered, textured or read by
+ * the CPU does not need CMA -- and must not take any, because CMA is a small
+ * fixed pool (dtoverlay=vc4-kms-v3d-pi4,cma-512) that is at the same time the
+ * only source of scanout memory. A 4K framebuffer needs 32 MiB of it in one
+ * piece, so letting ordinary GPU/CPU buffers fill and fragment the pool is what
+ * leaves a 4K display unable to allocate a framebuffer at all.
+ */
+#define V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED                                                                    \
+	(BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_DECODER | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER | BO_USE_CAMERA_READ |                   \
+	 BO_USE_CAMERA_WRITE | BO_USE_SENSOR_DIRECT_DATA)
+
+/*
+ * The display/cursor half: buffers a KMS plane would scan out. These are a SOFT
+ * requirement -- if CMA cannot satisfy them we still hand back a usable buffer,
+ * it just gets composited by the GPU instead of promoted to a hardware plane.
+ *
+ * On Android this set is deliberately EMPTY. fydroid's SurfaceFlinger is built
+ * with a factory that swaps HWComposer for a Wayland composer
+ * (FydroidSurfaceFlingerFactory.cpp) and no hwcomposer HAL is packaged, so
+ * Android never programs a KMS plane: every window buffer is exported as a
+ * dma-buf and handed to Chrome, which owns the display. But
+ * cros_gralloc_helpers.cc still maps GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_COMPOSER to
+ * BO_USE_SCANOUT | BO_USE_TEXTURE, and SurfaceFlinger sets that on essentially
+ * every layer -- the 4K surface that failed to allocate had usage 0xb00
+ * (HW_COMPOSER | HW_RENDER | HW_TEXTURE). Honouring SCANOUT here therefore puts
+ * *every ARC window buffer* in CMA, which is what exhausted the pool.
+ *
+ * This cannot be fixed in cros_gralloc_helpers.cc under #ifdef DRV_V3D:
+ * BOARD_MINIGBM_DRIVERS for fydroid-rt_arm64 is "rockchip v3d vc4 realtek", so
+ * a single image carries backends that do drive real scanout hardware and do
+ * depend on BO_USE_SCANOUT. The decision has to stay backend-local, here.
+ *
+ * To restore the old behaviour (e.g. if Chrome turns out to want ARC buffers on
+ * a hardware overlay after all), give this the non-Android definition.
+ */
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#define V3D_CONTIGUOUS_SOFT 0
+#else
+#define V3D_CONTIGUOUS_SOFT (BO_USE_SCANOUT | BO_USE_CURSOR)
+#endif
+
+#define V3D_CONTIGUOUS_USE (V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED | V3D_CONTIGUOUS_SOFT)
+
+/*
+ * UIF tiling is private to v3d. Any buffer the CPU maps or another device reads
+ * has to stay linear, whether or not it ends up in CMA -- dropping a buffer out
+ * of CMA must not change the layout its user already agreed to. Spelled out in
+ * full rather than derived from V3D_CONTIGUOUS_USE on purpose: narrowing what
+ * goes to CMA must never narrow what stays linear.
+ */
+#define V3D_LINEAR_USE                                                                             \
+	(BO_USE_NON_GPU_HW | BO_USE_CURSOR | BO_USE_SW_MASK | BO_USE_LINEAR |                       \
+	 BO_USE_GPU_DATA_BUFFER | BO_USE_RENDERSCRIPT | BO_USE_PROTECTED)
 
 enum v3d_tiling_mode {
         /* Untiled resources.  Not valid as texture inputs. */
@@ -257,6 +314,9 @@
 static int v3d_bo_create(struct bo *bo, uint32_t width, uint32_t height, uint32_t format,
        uint64_t use_flags) {
   struct v3d_driver_priv *dpriv = bo->drv->priv;
+  bool contiguous = use_flags & V3D_CONTIGUOUS_USE;
+  bool required = use_flags & V3D_CONTIGUOUS_REQUIRED;
+  bool linear = use_flags & V3D_LINEAR_USE;
   int ret;
   uint32_t stride, algin_height;
   struct drm_v3d_create_bo bo_create;
@@ -292,47 +352,62 @@
   bo->meta.total_size = ALIGN(bo->meta.total_size, 4096);
 
   /*
-   * Shared / scanout / CPU-visible buffers must be contiguous + linear.
-   * Prefer the CMA dma-heap (Option A); fall back to the legacy vc4 borrow
-   * only if the heap is unavailable.
+   * Only the buffers a non-GPU engine has to walk go to CMA; prefer the CMA
+   * dma-heap and fall back to the legacy vc4 borrow if the heap is absent.
    */
-  if (use_flags & V3D_HEAP_USE) {
-    if (dpriv && dpriv->heap_fd >= 0) {
-      struct v3d_bo_priv *bpriv = NULL;
-      ret = v3d_alloc_from_heap(bo, dpriv->heap_fd, &bpriv);
-      if (ret)
-        return ret;
+  if (contiguous && dpriv && dpriv->heap_fd >= 0) {
+    struct v3d_bo_priv *bpriv = NULL;
+    ret = v3d_alloc_from_heap(bo, dpriv->heap_fd, &bpriv);
+    if (!ret) {
       bo->priv = bpriv;
-      drv_logv("v3d bo path=CMA-HEAP  %ux%u %4s size=%zu mod=linear v3d_handle=0x%x dmabuf_fd=%d use=0x%llx\n",
+      drv_logv("v3d bo path=CMA-HEAP   %ux%u %4s size=%zu mod=linear v3d_handle=0x%x dmabuf_fd=%d use=0x%llx\n",
         width, height, (char *)&format, bo->meta.total_size, bo->handle.u32,
         bpriv->dmabuf_fd, (unsigned long long)use_flags);
       return 0;
     }
-    /* Legacy fallback: borrow a CMA BO from vc4 via the custom ioctl flag. */
-    bo_create.flags = ARC_CALLOC;
+    if (required)
+      return ret;
+    /* Display-only user: keep the buffer, lose the hardware plane. */
+    drv_logi("v3d: CMA heap cannot spare %zu bytes for a %ux%u %4s buffer (use=0x%llx); "
+      "falling back to pageable memory, it will be composited rather than scanned out\n",
+      bo->meta.total_size, width, height, (char *)&format, (unsigned long long)use_flags);
+    contiguous = false;
+  }
+
+  /*
+   * No dma-heap (older kernel, or the mapper copy which runs without the vendor
+   * SELinux permission), or the heap is exhausted: DRM_IOCTL_V3D_CREATE_BO.
+   * ARC_CALLOC makes v3d borrow the BO from vc4's CMA allocator; without it the
+   * BO is ordinary pageable memory behind the v3d MMU.
+   */
+  bo_create.size = bo->meta.total_size;
+  bo_create.flags = contiguous ? ARC_CALLOC : 0;
+  if (contiguous || linear) {
     bo->meta.format_modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR;
     bo->meta.tiling = V3D_TILING_RASTER;
-    drv_logv("v3d bo path=VC4-BORROW %ux%u %4s size=%zu mod=linear (no CMA dma-heap) use=0x%llx\n",
-      width, height, (char *)&format, bo->meta.total_size, (unsigned long long)use_flags);
   } else {
-    bo_create.flags = 0;
     bo->meta.format_modifier = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_UIF;
-    drv_logv("v3d bo path=V3D-UIF    %ux%u %4s size=%zu mod=uif (GPU-private) use=0x%llx\n",
-      width, height, (char *)&format, bo->meta.total_size, (unsigned long long)use_flags);
   }
 
-  bo_create.size = bo->meta.total_size;
   ret = drmIoctl(bo->drv->fd, DRM_IOCTL_V3D_CREATE_BO, &bo_create);
+  if (ret && contiguous && !required) {
+    drv_logi("v3d: vc4 CMA borrow of %zu bytes failed for a %ux%u %4s buffer (use=0x%llx); "
+      "retrying in pageable memory, it will be composited rather than scanned out\n",
+      bo->meta.total_size, width, height, (char *)&format, (unsigned long long)use_flags);
+    bo_create.flags = 0;
+    ret = drmIoctl(bo->drv->fd, DRM_IOCTL_V3D_CREATE_BO, &bo_create);
+  }
   if (ret) {
     drv_logv("DRM_IOCTL_V3D_CREATE_BO failed (size=%zu), ret=%d, format:%s\n", bo->meta.total_size, ret, (char *)&format);
     return -errno;
   }
 
   bo->handle.u32 = bo_create.handle;
-#ifdef DEBUG
- drv_logi("create v3d bo handler:0x%x, size:%zu, format:%4s, width:%u, height:%u, use_flags:0x%llx\n",
-   bo->handle.u32, bo->meta.total_size, (char *)&format, width, height, use_flags & (BO_USE_SW_MASK | BO_USE_SCANOUT));
-#endif
+  drv_logv("v3d bo path=%-11s %ux%u %4s size=%zu mod=%s v3d_handle=0x%x use=0x%llx\n",
+    bo_create.flags ? "VC4-BORROW" : (linear ? "V3D-LINEAR" : "V3D-UIF"),
+    width, height, (char *)&format, bo->meta.total_size,
+    (bo_create.flags || linear) ? "linear" : "uif", bo->handle.u32,
+    (unsigned long long)use_flags);
   return 0;
 }
 
